<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!--
  ONE FILE SERVES LUMA, HYVÄ AND CUSTOM THEMES.

  Module layout XML is theme-independent, and `head.additional` exists in Hyvä as
  well as Luma — so the widget is injected once here rather than per theme. That is
  what keeps two permanent storefront themes from becoming two of everything.

  NOTE WHAT IS ABSENT: there is no `cacheable="false"` on this block, and there must
  never be. On `default.xml` that attribute disables the full page cache for EVERY
  page of the store. The key-rotation problem it looks like a fix for is solved by
  the cache tag on the block instead — see Block\Storefront\Config.
-->
<page xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
      xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="urn:magento:framework:View/Layout/etc/page_configuration.xsd">
    <!--
      `head.additional` IS REFERENCED FROM <body>, NOT DECLARED INSIDE <head>.

      This is not a style choice and getting it wrong is not a soft failure. The
      page_configuration schema allows only title, css, link, meta, script, remove,
      attribute and font inside <head> — a <block> there fails XSD validation, and
      Magento's response to an invalid layout is to render an EXCEPTION PAGE FOR THE
      WHOLE STORE. Every page, not just this one. It was found here by noticing a
      7,405-byte "storefront" where a 200KB one belonged; the blob was correctly
      absent from it, which is exactly how a broken check reads as a passing one.

      `head.additional` is a BLOCK, not a container — `View\Result\Page` fetches it
      with `getLayout()->getBlock('head.additional')` and renders its html into the
      head. So it is referenced with `referenceBlock`. Using `referenceContainer` on
      it is a SILENT NO-OP: the layout validates, the page renders perfectly, and the
      block simply never appears. That cost a second round of debugging here, after
      the first one had already been blamed on caching.
    -->
    <body>
        <referenceBlock name="head.additional">
            <block class="NitroSearch\Search\Block\Storefront\Config"
                   name="nitrosearch.config"
                   template="NitroSearch_Search::storefront/config.phtml"/>
        </referenceBlock>
    </body>
</page>
